  "extra_findings": [
    "F5: export visibility. index.php?export=csv served every ticket to any logged-in session, clients included (index.php:44-47; exportarCsv reads the whole table). Real. The chosen fix, a 403 for every non-technician, is the COMP-003 charged to SEC-017's C5.",
    "F7: EXPORT_DIR '/var/www/painel/tmp' (config.php:17-18) may sit inside the document root, which would leave the full-table chamados.csv downloadable without login. Deployment-dependent, reported at confidence 60 with an operations action, not changed in code.",
    "F8: no rate limiting or lockout on login (index.php:21-29). Not fixed (needs new storage and a business policy).",
    "F11: non-atomic export. Concurrent exports reopen the shared chamados.csv with 'w' and truncate it while another request readfile()s it (lib.php:126 and :150). Fixed with php://temp, a uniquely named temp file and rename(). It lies at BUG-004's lines but does not describe the handle leak.",
    "F12: formatarStatus labels any status other than 1 and 2 as 'Resolvido' (lib.php:32-33). It calls the contracted legacy fallback a bug; the change to 'Desconhecido' is charged as COMP-003 (no C5).",
    "F15: rotuloPrioridade returns 'Aguardando 1a resposta' before looking at the priority, so priority-4 ticket 104 shows as an ordinary wait (lib.php:56-58). It calls contracted behaviour a bug; the behaviour is kept, so it is an extra (rule 14).",
    "SEC-005: no CSRF token on the login form (list of non-changes). Not fixed; the report judges it low risk."
